{"id":"000VPY","title":"Papolarity","author":"72kchunshuai","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-26T20:34:07+00:00","posted":"Heute, 21:13 Uhr","rules":"Recently I've been hooked on making Sudoku puzzles inspired by the mystery stories I read. The idea behind this one is simply that I noticed there are too many red-green colour-blind suspects in mystery stories. The difficulty is probably around 3.5*. Many thanks to cyddrdrd for testing!\n\nRules:\n\n• Normal Sudoku rules apply: Place the digits 1–9 once each in every row, column, and 3x3 box.\n\n• Grey lines:\n\n• A grey line is either a Parity line or a German Whisper line, to be deduced by the solver.\n\n• Digits along a grey line CANNOT repeat.\n\n• Parity lines: Adjacent digits along a red line must alternate between odd and even.\n\n• German Whispers: Adjacent digits along a green line must differ by at least 5.\n\nPlay on SudokuPad","solutionCode":"Row 8, from left to right, nine digits in total.","tags":["Sudoku","German Whispers (Variante)","Parity Party (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/xcexjq6oss","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/xcexjq6oss","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-26T20:34:07+00:00"}